(a) Report any suspected data breach to the Compliance Office immediately;
(b) The Compliance Office will assess the breach within 24 hours;
(c) GDPR breaches must be reported to the relevant supervisory authority within 72 hours;
(d) CCPA breaches requiring notification to affected individuals must be reported
without unreasonable delay.  PENALTIES
Non-compliance with these procedures may result in:
(a) Disciplinary action, up to and including termination;
(b) Personal liability for violations of GDPR (fines up to 4% of global revenue)
or CCPA (statutory damages of $100-$750 per consumer per incident);
(c) Referral to the relevant bar association for ethical violations.

2.  OBLIGATIONS OF RECEIVING PARTY
The Receiving Party agrees to:
(a) Hold the Confidential Information in strict confidence;
(b) Not disclose Confidential Information to any third party without prior written consent;
(c) Use the Confidential Information solely for the Purpose described herein;
(d) Apply reasonable security measures to protect Confidential Information from unauthorized access.

2.  ASSIGNMENT OF RIGHTS
Assignor hereby irrevocably assigns, transfers, and conveys to Assignee all right, title,
and interest in and to the Assigned IP, including:
(a) All patent rights, including the right to file and prosecute patent applications worldwide;
(b) All copyrights, including the right to reproduce, distribute, and create derivative works;
(c) All trade secret rights;
(d) All trademark rights associated with the Assigned IP;
(e) All rights to sue for past, present, and future infringement.

1.  GRANT OF AUTHORITY
I grant my Agent the following powers:
(a) Financial Management: To manage my bank accounts, investments, real property, and
personal property, including the power to buy, sell, lease, mortgage, and otherwise
deal with any property, real or personal;
(b) Tax Matters: To prepare, sign, and file tax returns, make estimated tax payments,
and represent me before the Internal Revenue Service and state tax authorities;
(c) Legal Proceedings: To commence, prosecute, discontinue, or defend any legal
proceedings on my behalf, including the power to retain counsel and settle claims;
(d) Government Benefits: To apply for and manage government benefits including Social
Security, Medicare, Medicaid, and veterans' benefits;
(e) Insurance: To procure, maintain, modify, or terminate insurance policies of any kind;
(f) Estate Planning: To create, amend, or revoke trusts and make gifts on my behalf,
subject to the limitations set forth in Section 4.

2.  HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION
We use collected information to:
(a) Provide, maintain, and improve the Service;
(b) Process and analyze documents submitted by users;
(c) Communicate with users about their accounts and service updates;
(d) Detect, prevent, and address technical issues and security threats;
(e) Comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms of service.

1.  SETTLEMENT PAYMENT
Defendant shall pay Plaintiff the total sum of $3,750,000 ("Settlement Amount") as follows:
(a) $2,000,000 within thirty (30) days of execution of this Agreement;
(b) $1,000,000 within ninety (90) days of execution;
(c) $750,000 within one hundred eighty (180) days of execution. 
Late payments shall accrue interest at a rate of 8% per annum.

